We are gearing up for a substantial production increase in the third quarter of this year and require precise planning for our material needs to prevent any shortages or overstock issues. Our product line includes multiple items, each with distinct lead times and specific supplier restrictions. We already have a compiled forecast for our production quantities along with the scheduled start dates for each product. Our current material inventory is accurately recorded, which will aid in determining how much more to order. Moreover, we've collected data on our suppliers' lead times for each material and are aware of the maximum delivery quantities they can provide per order. 

Could you please call the 'calculate_material_requirements' function with the relevant data to calculate the essential material quantities, considering the forecasted production increases and align them with our inventory levels? Additionally, it needs to accurately reflect the supplier lead times and their delivery constraints to ensure we have a well-structured material procurement plan.

Here's the data to use for the function call:

Production Forecast (JSON format):
```json
{
  "products": [
    {"product_id": "P001", "forecasted_quantity": 500, "production_start_date": "2023-07-01"},
    {"product_id": "P002", "forecasted_quantity": 300, "production_start_date": "2023-07-15"}
  ]
}
```

Current Inventory (JSON format):
```json
{
  "materials": [
    {"material_id": "M001", "available_quantity": 1000},
    {"material_id": "M002", "available_quantity": 1500}
  ]
}
```

