As the IT Procurement Manager for our company, I need to streamline and automate our procurement process for IT equipment and services. We plan to request quotes for various IT items from a selection of approved vendors. After obtaining these quotes, our aim is to compare them in terms of price and delivery times so we can choose the most favorable options. Once selected, we will generate the necessary purchase orders. Finally, we'll need a system to track each order's status until completion.

Our vendor list "vendors.json" contains names, contact information, and product categories for each vendor:

```json
[
  {
    "vendor_id": "V123",
    "company_name": "TechSupply Co.",
    "contact": {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "jdoe@techsupply.com"
    },
    "products_offered": ["Laptops", "Network Equipment"]
  },
  {
    "vendor_id": "V124",
    "company_name": "Enterprise IT Solutions",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Jane Smith",
      "email": "jsmith@enterpriseit.com"
    },
    "products_offered": ["Software Licenses", "Servers"]
  }
]
```

We also have a detailed list of the IT items we need quotes for in "items.json":

```json
[
  {
    "item_id": "I101",
    "description": "Laptop - High Performance",
    "specs": {
      "processor": "Intel Core i7",
      "memory": "16GB RAM",
      "storage": "512GB SSD"
    },
    "quantity": 15
  },
  {
    "item_id": "I102",
    "description": "Enterprise Server",
    "specs": {
      "processor": "Xeon E5 Series",
      "memory": "64GB RAM",
      "storage": "4TB HDD"
    },
    "quantity": 5
  }
]
```

I request to call the functions `request_quotes`, `compare_quotes`, `generate_purchase_orders`, and `track_order_status` using the data provided. This will help us execute each step of the IT procurement process more effectively. Use the details in the JSON files above as arguments for the function calls to facilitate this task. 

Please execute these functions as follows:
1. Call `request_quotes` with the "vendors.json" and "items.json" to request and collect quotes from our vendors.
2. Use `compare_quotes` to evaluate the received quotes once we have them.
3. After evaluation, call `generate_purchase_orders` for the selected quotes.
4. Lastly, use `track_order_status` to keep track of all the purchase orders we generate.
